          "author": {
            "displayName": "yuna5577",
            "tier": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "url": "/yuna5577"
          },
          "content": "<p>I looked at what actually separates the 18 models, using only train.csv and CPU.</p>\n<p>A few findings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The curly apostrophe (’) never appears in any Claude or GLM passage in train (0 of 567 passages that contain it).</li>\n<li>The em dash (—) almost never appears in Gemini (1 of 1,052 passages that contain it).</li>\n<li>Punctuation alone predicts the lab with 0.41 balanced accuracy (chance 0.17), but only 0.16 for the exact model.</li>\n<li>The hardest pairs are sibling versions (Gemini 3.7 vs 3.8 Flash, GPT-5.6 Luna vs Sol), plus Kimi vs GPT-5.5 and GLM-5.3 vs Claude Opus 5.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Notebook: <a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/yuna5577/name-that-llm-18-fingerprints\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kaggle.com/code/yuna5577/name-that-llm-18-fingerprints</a></p>\n<p>Feedback welcome, especially if anyone has checked whether these rules hold on the public LB.</p>",
          "id": 3544793,
          "isThankYou": false,
          "postDate": "2026-10-26T09:37:01.093Z",
